{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-topologies-section-introduction}", "REF_0002": "\\cite{Gr-I}", "REF_0003": "\\cite{Gr-II}", "REF_0004": "\\cite{Gr-III}", "REF_0005": "\\cite{Gr-IV}", "REF_0006": "\\cite{Gr-V}", "REF_0007": "\\cite{Gr-VI}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6005a58da3ecc643c1dc357aec15aae82738d8bc7053221717c46b3d309e0629", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the chapter on topologies on algebraic spaces (see\nTopologies on Spaces, Section <REF_0001>)\nwe introduced <ACCENT_0001>tale, fppf, smooth, syntomic and fpqc coverings of\nalgebraic spaces.\nIn this chapter we discuss what kind of structures over algebraic spaces\ncan be descended through such coverings.\nSee for example <REF_0002>, <REF_0003>, <REF_0004>,\n<REF_0005>, <REF_0006>, and <REF_0007>.\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:46ccef44823190f57f1299b9dc8128b4c8caadc1a9cc8a3b03240d441ba0182d", "unit_id": "tag:03YF:prose-0001"}
